ther, computers). Concerns: communication tone, pretentiousness may affect crew cooperation.\n\nCandidate C: dossier: makes correct decisions quickly, difficulty communicating ideas, egocentric, not willing to further education. Private: puts concern for others above everything, excellent attention skills. Strengths: decision quality, attention, caring for others (crew cooperation). Concerns: communication difficulty, egocentric, lack of development.\n\nCandidate D: dossier: responds to unexpected events adequately, concentrates well, solves problems extremely well, takes responsibility seriously. Private: moody, loner. Strengths: adaptability, attention, problem solving, responsibility. Concerns: moodiness, loner may affect crew cooperation.\n\nWe need initial recommendation. Which candidate best overall? Candidate B has strong reliability, stress, technical, but communication issues. Candidate D has strong problem solving, responsibility, attention, but moodiness and loner may affect crew cooperation. Candidate C has decision quality, attention, caring, but communication issues and egocentric, not willing to learn. Candidate A has technical, leadership, but unfriendly and unhealthy (maybe reliability). I'd lean towards Candidate B as overall strong, but need to consider crew cooperation. Both B and D have concerns. Maybe B slightly better because stress handling is crucial for long-distance. So initial vote Candidate B.\n\nWe should share some evidence: mention B's strengths and concerns. Also note missing info: we haven't heard about B's adaptability/feedback orientation. Could ask other panel for that. But as first turn, we can give recommendation and highlight evidence.\n\nThus PUBLIC_MESSAGE: give recommendation, summarize strengths and concerns, note need for more info on crew cooperation and adaptability.\n\nMETADATA_JSON vote B."}
