ty, no feedback openness.\n\nNow as agent 2, need to contribute next. We have private notes: A show-off, not open to new ideas; B weak memory for numbers, nasty remarks; C keeps calm in crisis, understands complicated technology; D know-it-all, hot temper. Also we have shared evidence.\n\nWe need to make a concise professional contribution: maybe compare candidates on crew cooperation and communication, given new info. Or highlight concerns about B's communication (nasty remarks) and D's temperament, and C's positive crew atmosphere but communication difficulty. Could propose focusing on crew cooperation and communication as key unresolved criteria.\n\nWe also need to give our vote. Based on evidence, we might still lean B but need to consider crew cooperation issues. D has temperament issues; C has communication difficulty; A has show-off and not open to ideas. B has nasty remarks, weak numeric memory (attention). Which is most critical? For long-distance, reliability, stress, technical competence, decision quality, attention, crew cooperation, communication, responsibility, adaptability.\n\nB: strong reliability, stress, technical, but communication issues (nasty remarks) and weak numeric memory (attention). D: strong problem solving, responsibility, attention, but moody, loner (crew cooperation). C: good decision, calm, technical, crew cooperation positive, but communication difficulty, egocentric, not willing to learn. A: technical, leadership, but show-off, not open to ideas, maybe reliability questionable.\n\nWhich candidate best overall? Might be C: calm, good decision, crew cooperation positive, technical, but communication difficulty and egocentric. However egocentric could affect crew. B's nasty remarks also affect crew. D's temperament also.\n\nWe could suggest that we need more info on B's numeric memory impact and D's teamwork, maybe ask about B's numeric memory effect on tasks. But we already have note: weak memory for numbers. Could ask about how critical that is.\n\nBut the next contribution could be to compare B and D on crew cooperation and communication, highlighting that both have concerns, and propose focusing on which is more severe.\n\nWe also need to give our vote. I think provisional vote could be Candidate C? Let's weigh: reliability? Not explicit but from dossier: not mentioned. Private notes: no reliability concerns. Dossier: not mention reliability. B is very conscientious (reliability). C not mentioned. So reliability maybe lower for C. Stress resilience: C keeps calm in crisis (good). B handles stress well (good). Decision quality: C makes correct decisions quickly (good). B not mentioned. Technical competence: C understands complicated technology (good). B good at weather, computer. Attention: D concentrates well, solves problems. B weak numeric memory (attention). Crew cooperation: C positive atmosphere, B nasty remarks, D moody/loner, A show-off.\n\nThus C seems balanced but communication difficulty and egocentric may affect crew. But crew cooperation positive suggests maybe can work.\n\nGiven the panel, maybe we should keep provisional recommendation B but note concerns. Or shift to C? Need to decide.\n\nI think we can state that after reviewing crew cooperation and communication, Candidate C shows strong crew cooperation and calmness, while B has communication issues. D has temperament issues. A has leadership but interpersonal concerns. Therefore C emerges as strong alternative. I might vote for Candidate C.\n\nLet's produce contribution: summarize new info, compare, and give provisional vote for C, with rationale."}
